---
scope: src/tools/upgrade/buildVersionsMeta
status: aligned
description: >
  Build-time script that generates a complete versions.json manifest covering every shipped AIDE artifact category, baked into the published npm package as a static asset.
intent: >
  buildVersionsMeta is a build-time script that produces a versions.json
  manifest containing version metadata for every artifact the MCP server
  delivers to host projects. The manifest is generated during the npm
  publish pipeline, baked into the package as a static asset, and read
  by the install and upgrade surfaces at runtime. Host projects never
  need access to the MCP server's git history or source repo; the
  manifest travels with the package.
outcomes:
  desired:
    - versions.json covers every shipped artifact category that the install and upgrade surfaces deliver to host projects, with no category silently omitted.
    - Each entry carries enough metadata to identify the version of that artifact (publication timestamp, source commit reference) so consuming tools can detect drift between what the host has and what the package ships.
    - The manifest is generated at build time during the npm publish pipeline and embedded into the published package as a static file — never computed at runtime on the client machine.
    - Both install and upgrade surfaces read the same shipped manifest to deliver version metadata to host projects, so version reporting is consistent across delivery channels.
  undesired:
    - Runtime dependency on git availability or the MCP server's repo history on the client machine. Clients install from npm and have no access to the source repo's git log.
    - Coverage limited to a subset of shipped artifact categories. A manifest that tracks only part of the delivery surface is incomplete and will miss drift in the artifacts it does not cover.
    - An empty or partial versions.json reaching published packages because the build script failed silently or was skipped in the publish pipeline.
    - The install surface delivering artifacts without version metadata while the upgrade surface delivers it. Both channels must use the same manifest.
---
